  "blocks": [
    {
      "block_id": 0,
      "type": 0,
      "text": "Each of the DMA channels can be independently enabled or disabled. The enable bits are bits \nSRCA, SRCB, SRCC, and DEST in control register zero (BLTCONO).\n",
      "bbox": [
        82.9000015258789,
        56.22502899169922,
        514.3975219726562,
        79.42400360107422
      ],
      "bbox_norm": [
        0.13797579875820792,
        0.07284167051358631,
        0.8561448451995982,
        0.10289682735483276
      ]
    },
    {
      "block_id": 1,
      "type": 0,
      "text": "When disabled, no memory cycles will be executed for that channel and, for a source channel, the \nconstant value stored in the data register of that channel will be used for each blitter cycle. For \nthis purpose, each of the three source channels have preloadable data registers, called BLTxDAT.\n",
      "bbox": [
        82.9000015258789,
        94.97301483154297,
        515.1848754882812,
        130.9730224609375
      ],
      "bbox_norm": [
        0.13797579875820792,
        0.12304116472865735,
        0.8574552882421057,
        0.1696805483137524
      ]
    },
    {
      "block_id": 2,
      "type": 0,
      "text": "Images in memory are usually stored in a linear fashion; each word of data on a line is located a t, \nan address that is one greater than the word on its left. i.e. Each line is a “ plus one” continua­\ntion of the previous line. (See Figure 6-1.)\n",
      "bbox": [
        82.9000015258789,
        145.7230224609375,
        519.9500122070312,
        182.02001953125
      ],
      "bbox_norm": [
        0.13797579875820792,
